    model_how: "<b>How do we know how much each piece of data counts?</b> That piece of data is swapped for the one of an ordinary hour, and we look at how much the percentage changes. Example for this hour: if “{name}” were that of an ordinary hour, the percentage {dir} by about {x}%; that is why it shows {v}. The numbers are rounded, so their sum may be 1% off.",
